WEBVTT

1
00:47:38.562 --> 00:47:47.562
I want to sing once. Bend, I want to ask if Caroline, maybe Sammy and Cindy, the three of you, I don't care who, but can you please sing this a cappella?

2
00:47:47.562 --> 00:47:55.562
Blessed, I want to ask you to stand, close your eyes and focus on this refrain.

3
00:47:55.562 --> 00:48:04.562
Lord, I give you my heart. When the band sings this, I want to ask to do it a cappella as a statement, as a silence statement.

4
00:48:04.562 --> 00:48:10.562
For sometimes the music fills the room and your focus is on the song because of the symphony of the song.

5
00:48:10.562 --> 00:48:15.562
And then you are so into the melody and it is so beautiful and so well composed.

6
00:48:15.562 --> 00:48:21.562
And the sea of sound, the symphony of the whole song, is then the song itself.

7
00:48:21.562 --> 00:48:29.562
But I want to focus on the words themselves and I want to ask us as a church to focus on the prayer of the words sung a cappella.

8
00:48:29.562 --> 00:48:36.562
And I want to ask you to mean this with all your heart. Come now to repentance and sing these words to God. Carolinko.

9
00:48:59.562 --> 00:49:10.562
Do your will in me. Lord, I give you my heart. I give you my soul.

10
00:49:10.562 --> 00:49:23.562
I live only for you. Lead the way that I go. Every moment until I exist.

11
00:49:24.562 --> 00:49:42.562
Lord, do your will in me. Lord, do your will in me. Lord, do your will in me.

12
00:49:42.562 --> 00:49:51.562
Lord, give Jesus a round of applause. Let yourself cheer for him. Hallelujah. Praise your name Jesus. Do your will in me.

13
00:49:51.562 --> 00:49:58.562
Hallelujah. Can we close our eyes? Hallelujah. King Jesus.

14
00:49:58.562 --> 00:50:04.562
King Jesus. Lord, I give you my heart. Lord, I want to pray this for the people in this room.

15
00:50:05.562 --> 00:50:15.562
Lord, we give our hearts to you. Lord, I want to pray at this moment for the people who want to give their hearts, but have obstacles.

16
00:50:15.562 --> 00:50:20.562
Lord, I want to pray that there will be total freedom in this room in the name of Jesus.

17
00:50:20.562 --> 00:50:26.562
That we can give our hearts to you in worship. That we can give our hearts when reaching out to God.

18
00:50:26.562 --> 00:50:29.562
That we can give our hearts throughout the week.

19
00:50:29.562 --> 00:50:33.562
Lord, when we go to our jobs. Lord, when we have free time.

20
00:50:33.562 --> 00:50:37.562
Sometimes maybe not even knowing what we should do as an outlet.

21
00:50:37.562 --> 00:50:42.562
Lord, that you are our outlet. That you are our relax. That you are our chill-out.

22
00:50:42.562 --> 00:50:46.562
Lord, that we can say, do your will in me.

23
00:50:46.562 --> 00:50:51.562
Lord, I want to pray that these words will be taken seriously in this church.

24
00:50:51.562 --> 00:50:56.562
I give you my soul. Such weight on these words. I give you my soul.

25
00:50:56.562 --> 00:51:01.562
But Lord, you are worth our soul. You are so worth it.

26
00:51:01.562 --> 00:51:07.562
There is only one person who is worth our soul. One person.

27
00:51:07.562 --> 00:51:12.562
You are not even worth your own soul, because we have squandered it.

28
00:51:12.562 --> 00:51:16.562
But Jesus is worth it, because He has restored our soul.

29
00:51:16.562 --> 00:51:21.562
He is amazing. He is the King. He is the Lord of Lords.

30
00:51:21.562 --> 00:51:24.562
He is my Savior. He is my very best friend.

31
00:51:24.562 --> 00:51:29.562
I have no other very best friends. All respect for all my friends.

32
00:51:29.562 --> 00:51:33.562
But He is the very best friend. You can truly rely on Him.

33
00:51:33.562 --> 00:51:37.562
He will never have a down day. He is the King of Kings.

34
00:51:37.562 --> 00:51:41.562
He stands on this world as His footstool.

35
00:51:41.562 --> 00:51:46.562
He is so powerful that He created heaven and earth. The universe belongs to Him.

36
00:51:46.562 --> 00:51:49.562
And He wants to be my personal friend.

37
00:51:50.562 --> 00:51:52.562
This is amazing, guys.

38
00:51:52.562 --> 00:51:54.562
He wants to be your friend.

39
00:51:54.562 --> 00:51:57.562
The only thing He asks is a song.

40
00:51:57.562 --> 00:52:00.562
That is the only thing. A melody in your heart.

41
00:52:00.562 --> 00:52:03.562
That you give yourself to Him and that you mean it. Hallelujah.

42
00:52:03.562 --> 00:52:07.562
Just give the person next to you a hug or a high-five.

43
00:52:07.562 --> 00:52:11.562
Say for a moment, you are welcome in the name of Jesus.

44
00:52:11.562 --> 00:52:14.562
You are welcome in the name of Jesus.

45
00:52:19.562 --> 00:52:22.562
Hallelujah.

46
00:52:33.562 --> 00:52:37.562
Say it to the person next to you.

47
00:52:37.562 --> 00:52:40.562
You are welcome in the name of Jesus.

48
00:52:40.562 --> 00:52:43.562
Welcome each other.

49
00:52:49.562 --> 00:52:56.562
Hallelujah.

50
00:52:56.562 --> 00:53:05.562
If you have greeted or blessed someone, you may sit down for a moment.

51
00:53:05.562 --> 00:53:10.562
Hallelujah.

52
00:53:10.562 --> 00:53:18.562
It is not an earthly question to ask if you enjoyed the worship.

53
00:53:18.562 --> 00:53:25.562
If you come into the same wavelength as God, He can enjoy us and we can enjoy Him.

54
00:53:25.562 --> 00:53:28.562
Amen.

55
00:53:28.562 --> 00:53:32.562
I have heard in the pathways that you are getting married.

56
00:53:32.562 --> 00:53:35.562
Is that true?

57
00:53:35.562 --> 00:53:37.562
Congratulations, boy.

58
00:53:37.562 --> 00:53:42.562
Congratulations.

59
00:53:42.562 --> 00:53:45.562
You have chosen a handsome one.

60
00:53:46.562 --> 00:53:49.562
You have chosen a handsome one.

61
00:53:49.562 --> 00:53:52.562
Good job.

62
00:53:52.562 --> 00:53:57.562
Church, listen.

63
00:53:57.562 --> 00:54:06.562
A few years ago, we received a kind of prophecy as a church.

64
00:54:06.562 --> 00:54:19.562
That means that someone receives a word or a thought that he or she believes and trusts from the relationship that person has with God.

65
00:54:19.562 --> 00:54:23.562
Intimate communication, then you can receive something from God that you know.

66
00:54:23.562 --> 00:54:28.562
And then you say in respect and humility, I feel that God said this.

67
00:54:28.562 --> 00:54:38.562
That is called a prophecy, when you manage to receive the heart of the Father and you can communicate that in our language and then pass it on to someone.

68
00:54:38.562 --> 00:54:40.562
That is giving a prophetic word.

69
00:54:40.562 --> 00:54:49.562
And over this church, a prophetic word was spoken a number of years ago and I can’t quite remember who exactly said it.

70
00:54:49.562 --> 00:54:55.562
Annie, if you know, you may say it, but it doesn’t matter, because the words themselves were very important.

71
00:54:55.562 --> 00:55:04.562
And it was that this church would be a church where people from other countries would come through our church.

72
00:55:04.562 --> 00:55:05.562
Right?

73
00:55:05.562 --> 00:55:07.562
Was that you?

74
00:55:07.562 --> 00:55:09.562
An in-house prophet.

75
00:55:09.562 --> 00:55:13.562
No, but I think Steven Rieta said it too, namely.

76
00:55:13.562 --> 00:55:17.562
That resources and people would come to our church.

77
00:55:18.562 --> 00:55:32.562
Do you know what you need to do, church? You always need to look at what God intended as a task for you individually or for us as a church.

78
00:55:32.562 --> 00:55:41.562
And the success of a church, of a household in Christ, is measured by what we do according to the will of the Father.

79
00:55:41.562 --> 00:55:43.562
That is where success lies.

80
00:55:43.562 --> 00:55:48.562
Success is not measured by the number of euros we have in the bank.

81
00:55:48.562 --> 00:55:52.562
Success is not measured by the number of people who come to church.

82
00:55:52.562 --> 00:55:58.562
Success is not even measured by the number of people you baptize over the course of a year.

83
00:55:58.562 --> 00:56:00.562
Yes, of course we want to baptize many people.

84
00:56:00.562 --> 00:56:12.562
But John the Baptist proves by saying it doesn't matter how many people I baptize compared to how many people Jesus himself baptized in his time.

85
00:56:12.562 --> 00:56:16.562
For Jesus attracted more attention than John the Baptist.

86
00:56:16.562 --> 00:56:21.562
But John the Baptist says success is not dependent on the number of people I baptize.

87
00:56:21.562 --> 00:56:28.562
Success is dependent on whether I do what the Father desires me to do.

88
00:56:28.562 --> 00:56:31.562
That is what it means to be a successful Christian.

89
00:56:32.562 --> 00:56:42.562
And as I learn in this church and then through various words that we as a church may be a hub.

90
00:56:42.562 --> 00:56:51.562
A hub, H-U-B, an English word that means a gathering place where we see people passing through.

91
00:56:51.562 --> 00:57:00.562
Rick Warren once said, the success of a church is not by its seating capacity but by its sending capacity.

92
00:57:00.562 --> 00:57:05.562
In other words, equipping Christians with the holy tools from Scripture.

93
00:57:05.562 --> 00:57:10.562
And then sending them out so they can be the people of God in this world.

94
00:57:10.562 --> 00:57:17.562
You know what I find so beautiful is that last week Ashkan and Helia our brother and sister from Iran.

95
00:57:17.562 --> 00:57:21.562
Where are you today? Somewhere hidden in the dark. Give a wave.

96
00:57:21.562 --> 00:57:28.562
There you are. They have been coming to our church for the past week and a few weeks before that.

97
00:57:28.562 --> 00:57:37.562
And last week we felt led to pray for this power couple because they are committed to the church in Iran and also in Turkey.

98
00:57:37.562 --> 00:57:43.562
They are committed to the church and sometimes you sing a song that we just sang.

99
00:57:43.562 --> 00:57:49.562
Even though I don't know what the solution is, you are still at work. I see you do it.

100
00:57:49.562 --> 00:57:56.562
And sometimes I think to myself how can Iran and how can Turkey with such an earthquake I think to myself.

101
00:57:56.562 --> 00:58:01.562
How can that ever be rebuilt? It is a country that struggles with finances.

102
00:58:01.562 --> 00:58:06.562
And then you have an earthquake on such a scale and everything goes down.

103
00:58:06.562 --> 00:58:10.562
Do you know what it costs to rebuild that? I have no answer to that.

104
00:58:10.562 --> 00:58:15.562
But the church of Jesus has an answer to that and His name is Jesus. Amen.

105
00:58:15.562 --> 00:58:21.562
And you know what I find so great is that we as a church take this calling seriously.

106
00:58:21.562 --> 00:58:28.562
And that we opened our wallets last week and raised 4500 euros for this couple.

107
00:58:28.562 --> 00:58:33.562
And that is a large amount. And we are going to bless you with that.

108
00:58:33.562 --> 00:58:40.562
You will be blessed with this amount and Debbie or Bram will contact you about how we can give that.

109
00:58:40.562 --> 00:58:45.562
But this is something that you as a church can be happy about.

110
00:58:45.562 --> 00:58:51.562
And towards Jesus that you can be proud and being proud can also be a good thing.

111
00:58:51.562 --> 00:58:56.562
So you can be proud of who we are allowed to be in Christ. That is good pride.

112
00:58:56.562 --> 00:59:02.562
Be glad that you know who you are in Christ. Be glad that you know that you walk in His light.

113
00:59:02.562 --> 00:59:07.562
Be glad that you can recognize His footsteps and that you can stand in them.

114
00:59:07.562 --> 00:59:10.562
And that is being proud in a good way. You should never be proud towards yourself.

115
00:59:10.562 --> 00:59:14.562
Like look at what we can do. It doesn't matter what we can do.

116
00:59:14.562 --> 00:59:18.562
It is about what He can do. Amen. Hallelujah.

117
00:59:18.562 --> 00:59:22.562
Praise the name of Jesus. Hallelujah. I'm happy.

118
00:59:22.562 --> 00:59:24.562
Bram, may I invite you?

119
00:59:26.562 --> 00:59:28.562
May I have a round of applause for our elder?

120
00:59:30.562 --> 00:59:33.562
He is not the oldest, but he is indeed the elder.

121
00:59:38.562 --> 00:59:41.562
May I have the text?

122
00:59:46.562 --> 00:59:50.562
This is a piece from the Old Testament. Just a few verses.

123
00:59:53.562 --> 01:00:00.562
At that time, God chose to be with the people and to make that very visible

124
01:00:00.562 --> 01:00:04.562
by taking place in a tent and later in the temple.

125
01:00:04.562 --> 01:00:07.562
God who wants to be with the people.

126
01:00:07.562 --> 01:00:11.562
And here Solomon writes a letter.

127
01:00:11.562 --> 01:00:17.562
And he writes, Solomon is the king who built the first great temple.

128
01:00:17.562 --> 01:00:23.562
And he writes here, I am going to build a very large temple for him.

129
01:00:23.562 --> 01:00:29.562
For our God is greater and more powerful than all other gods.

130
01:00:30.562 --> 01:00:34.562
Actually, no one can build a temple for him.

131
01:00:34.562 --> 01:00:38.562
For the heavens, even the highest heaven, are still too small for him.

132
01:00:38.562 --> 01:00:44.562
Actually, he says, I do have plans to build a great temple, but actually it is a bit invisible.

133
01:00:46.562 --> 01:00:51.562
God, he does not need me to build a temple for him at all.

134
01:00:51.562 --> 01:00:57.562
But I want to do that in order to bring him offerings.

135
01:00:58.562 --> 01:01:04.562
Today, God no longer has a need for a stone building.

136
01:01:04.562 --> 01:01:11.562
Today, we as a church are the building where he resides.

137
01:01:11.562 --> 01:01:16.562
The place where he lives.

138
01:01:16.562 --> 01:01:20.562
This is a letter, actually that is wonderful.

139
01:01:20.562 --> 01:01:24.562
This is a letter, this is simply international history.

140
01:01:24.562 --> 01:01:29.562
This is about international trade relations, about who may buy what from whom.

141
01:01:29.562 --> 01:01:33.562
And it is also about exchanging high-quality technological knowledge.

142
01:01:33.562 --> 01:01:37.562
There is nothing new under the sun from time to time, you know.

143
01:01:37.562 --> 01:01:45.562
And Solomon asks for the delivery of building materials and whether there is a craftsman who can help him from his neighboring country.

144
01:01:46.562 --> 01:01:50.562
Then he explains what his plan is.

145
01:01:50.562 --> 01:01:55.562
Then he also explains who God is.

146
01:01:55.562 --> 01:02:00.562
And then he says, God does not need it at all.

147
01:02:00.562 --> 01:02:04.562
God does not need our money.

148
01:02:04.562 --> 01:02:08.562
Yet we are going to hold a collection now.

149
01:02:09.562 --> 01:02:13.562
Collection for the church itself.

150
01:02:13.562 --> 01:02:17.562
For the growth, the building, the functioning of the church.

151
01:02:17.562 --> 01:02:21.562
Also just for the daily expenses.

152
01:02:21.562 --> 01:02:25.562
Gas, water, electricity, salaries all just continue.

153
01:02:25.562 --> 01:02:28.562
Part of our functioning.

154
01:02:28.562 --> 01:02:32.562
Part of the healthy functioning of the church.

155
01:02:33.562 --> 01:02:40.562
The motive is, God does not need it, it is his church.

156
01:02:40.562 --> 01:02:43.562
He can take care of everything anyway.

157
01:02:43.562 --> 01:02:51.562
But, we say, I want to do that.

158
01:02:51.562 --> 01:02:55.562
I want to contribute.

159
01:02:55.562 --> 01:02:58.562
I want to give to God.

160
01:02:58.562 --> 01:03:02.562
I want to bring an offering for him.

161
01:03:02.562 --> 01:03:06.562
Are you welcome to do that now? Thank you.

162
01:03:07.562 --> 01:03:11.562
APPLAUSE

163
01:03:26.562 --> 01:03:28.562
Hallelujah.

164
01:03:28.562 --> 01:03:31.562
Would you like to stand once more?

165
01:03:31.562 --> 01:03:33.562
Amen.

166
01:03:33.562 --> 01:03:37.562
Hallelujah, Lord, we love you.

167
01:03:37.562 --> 01:03:40.562
Jesus, you are faithful.

168
01:03:40.562 --> 01:03:43.562
Faithful in every season.

169
01:03:43.562 --> 01:03:48.562
Thank you for being faithful and true.

170
01:03:48.562 --> 01:03:55.562
Holy Spirit, come to our hearts today.

171
01:03:55.562 --> 01:03:58.562
And bring the Word to us.

172
01:03:58.562 --> 01:04:03.562
Make a transformation in our hearts.

173
01:04:03.562 --> 01:04:07.562
I ask this in the name of Jesus.

174
01:04:07.562 --> 01:04:10.562
That the Lord may have His way.

175
01:04:10.562 --> 01:04:12.562
Amen.

176
01:04:12.562 --> 01:04:15.562
Thank you, Ben.

177
01:04:15.562 --> 01:04:21.562
Feel free to sit down, do you have your Bible with you?

178
01:04:21.562 --> 01:04:26.562
Then grab your Bible, because you need it.

179
01:04:27.562 --> 01:04:31.562
I see no one grabbing a Bible.

180
01:04:31.562 --> 01:04:36.562
Is there anyone who is grabbing a Bible?

181
01:04:36.562 --> 01:04:40.562
Keep it in the air if you have one.

182
01:04:40.562 --> 01:04:43.562
Not enough, more.

183
01:04:43.562 --> 01:04:46.562
Paper Bible, amen.

184
01:04:46.562 --> 01:04:49.562
We are very religious.

185
01:04:49.562 --> 01:04:52.562
No, I'm joking.

186
01:04:52.562 --> 01:04:55.562
It's better, amen.

187
01:04:56.562 --> 01:05:00.562
I don't know, but it's better.

188
01:05:00.562 --> 01:05:02.562
I will continue.

189
01:05:02.562 --> 01:05:05.562
I think I talked about this teaching about four weeks ago.

190
01:05:05.562 --> 01:05:09.562
the beginning of this teaching.

191
01:05:09.562 --> 01:05:12.562
Amen.

192
01:05:12.562 --> 01:05:17.562
It's about living in the light of eternity

193
01:05:17.562 --> 01:05:20.562
and the eternal reward.

194
01:05:20.562 --> 01:05:24.562
Does anyone still remember where we started?

195
01:05:25.562 --> 01:05:28.562
I will summarize it quickly for you.

196
01:05:35.562 --> 01:05:39.562
Jesus and the apostles talk repeatedly about eternity

197
01:05:39.562 --> 01:05:42.562
and about the eternal reward.

198
01:05:44.562 --> 01:05:49.562
And very specifically about the judgment stream of God.

199
01:05:50.562 --> 01:05:54.562
When Jesus returns the second time.

200
01:06:00.562 --> 01:06:04.562
And that reality of a reward in eternity.

201
01:06:04.562 --> 01:06:08.562
is really a positive motivation for us.

202
01:06:09.562 --> 01:06:13.562
It truly aims to motivate you

203
01:06:13.562 --> 01:06:18.562
to chase after everything that is available in that salvation in Christ.

204
01:06:27.562 --> 01:06:31.562
Do we understand that such a perspective on eternity

205
01:06:31.562 --> 01:06:35.562
brings us a motivation that is not available in any other way?

206
01:06:39.562 --> 01:06:41.562
Let me put it this way.

207
01:06:41.562 --> 01:06:44.562
If you think that life is really just temporary

208
01:06:44.562 --> 01:06:48.562
then you will always make choices that are short-term

209
01:06:48.562 --> 01:06:56.562
a gratification, what did I say?

210
01:06:56.562 --> 01:06:59.562
Providing short-term satisfaction, thank you Chris.

211
01:07:00.562 --> 01:07:03.562
If we believe that it is only about this

212
01:07:03.562 --> 01:07:05.562
then we will make lesser choices

213
01:07:05.562 --> 01:07:09.562
than when we keep our eyes focused on that eternity.

214
01:07:13.562 --> 01:07:16.562
So let me tell you in another way.

215
01:07:16.562 --> 01:07:19.562
The eternal reward in eternity

216
01:07:19.562 --> 01:07:23.562
is really a positive motivation for us.

217
01:07:23.562 --> 01:07:26.562
It truly aims to motivate you

218
01:07:27.562 --> 01:07:31.562
So let me say it to you again, this is a good message.

219
01:07:32.562 --> 01:07:34.562
You want to hear this.

220
01:07:39.562 --> 01:07:42.562
And I also said it at the Leaders' Weekend.

221
01:07:42.562 --> 01:07:45.562
If we ignore something, it does not make it any less true.

222
01:07:49.562 --> 01:07:53.562
You can ignore things in the Bible, but that does not make them any less true.

223
01:07:54.562 --> 01:07:58.562
Ignoring it only means that you yourself do not know it.

224
01:08:06.562 --> 01:08:09.562
And the Bible is so full of this reality.

225
01:08:09.562 --> 01:08:11.562
Jesus really wants us to understand this.

226
01:08:13.562 --> 01:08:15.562
So it is a good message.

227
01:08:18.562 --> 01:08:22.562
It may bring a bit of fear of the Lord, but you know, that is good for you.

228
01:08:24.562 --> 01:08:28.562
That keeps you spiritually fit.

229
01:08:35.562 --> 01:08:37.562
I want to go back to the first text.

230
01:08:37.562 --> 01:08:39.562
Then we go to 2 Corinthians 9.

231
01:08:43.562 --> 01:08:45.562
And Paul writes here.

232
01:08:53.562 --> 01:08:55.562
Then it is written.

233
01:09:01.562 --> 01:09:03.562
2 Corinthians 5 verse 9.

234
01:09:09.562 --> 01:09:12.562
So we make it our goal to please Him.

235
01:09:15.562 --> 01:09:18.562
Whether we are at home in the body or away from it.

236
01:09:19.562 --> 01:09:20.562
Verse 10.

237
01:09:22.562 --> 01:09:24.562
And then in verse 10 is the reason.

238
01:09:28.562 --> 01:09:30.562
For we must all.

239
01:09:33.562 --> 01:09:37.562
We must all appear before the judgment seat of Jesus.

240
01:09:37.562 --> 01:09:39.562
And this is for the Christian.

241
01:10:00.562 --> 01:10:05.562
I am not talking about a judgment on sin, for you are forgiven by Jesus.

242
01:10:05.562 --> 01:10:13.562
But I am talking about the assessment of what you have done and the gifts He wants to give to that.

243
01:10:16.562 --> 01:10:18.562
So that each of us.

244
01:10:20.562 --> 01:10:22.562
May receive what he deserves.

245
01:10:26.562 --> 01:10:28.562
For the things he has done in his life.

246
01:10:29.562 --> 01:10:31.562
Whether they are good or bad.

247
01:10:36.562 --> 01:10:40.562
Even as a person who is saved, you can still make good and bad choices.

248
01:10:43.562 --> 01:10:45.562
But we can choose the good things.

249
01:10:50.562 --> 01:10:56.562
What Tim just said, we can choose to do those things that are in line with God's will for our lives.

250
01:10:57.562 --> 01:11:01.562
So Paul says, the purpose of salvation is to please the Lord in this life.

251
01:11:06.562 --> 01:11:08.562
And that makes it very simple.

252
01:11:15.562 --> 01:11:20.562
If you have an attitude, I just want to please the Lord, that brings a lot of clarity.

253
01:11:27.562 --> 01:11:32.562
And we know from Hebrews 11 that faith pleases the Lord.

254
01:11:37.562 --> 01:11:42.562
And He even turns it around, He says without faith it is impossible to please God.

255
01:11:47.562 --> 01:11:52.562
In other words, our works, the deeds that we do, we do them in faith.

256
01:11:57.562 --> 01:12:03.562
And Paul reasons that because he and everyone must appear before that throne.

257
01:12:10.562 --> 01:12:14.562
Then he wants to use his time on earth to be useful to the Lord.

258
01:12:17.562 --> 01:12:19.562
Useful in faithfulness.

259
01:12:27.562 --> 01:12:36.562
And here we will continue today, we will go to Matthew 25 and we will look at the usefulness and availability of the servant.

260
01:12:46.562 --> 01:12:51.562
And another verse that we mentioned last time also comes from Corinthians, that is Corinthians 3 verse 10.

261
01:12:57.562 --> 01:13:07.562
And there it stands, by the grace that God has given me, I have laid a foundation as a wise builder.

262
01:13:10.562 --> 01:13:12.562
And someone else builds upon it.

263
01:13:14.562 --> 01:13:17.562
But each one must build with care.

264
01:13:17.562 --> 01:13:28.562
For no one can lay another foundation than that which is already laid, and that is Jesus Christ himself.

265
01:13:38.562 --> 01:13:45.562
And this is true for his ministry, he has laid the foundation of Christ who was crucified, and others build upon it.

266
01:13:47.562 --> 01:13:49.562
But it is also true in our lives.

267
01:13:58.562 --> 01:14:05.562
Jesus Christ crucified for me, that is the foundation upon which my faith is built.

268
01:14:06.562 --> 01:14:08.562
But it is not yet a complete house.

269
01:14:09.562 --> 01:14:11.562
He says, and now, go and build.

270
01:14:11.562 --> 01:14:20.562
I said it a few weeks ago, nowhere in the Bible do you see, be saved and now just sit down comfortably.

271
01:14:23.562 --> 01:14:27.562
Has anyone taken on challenges, have you found the verse?

272
01:14:30.562 --> 01:14:33.562
Be saved, sit down, do nothing more.

273
01:14:35.562 --> 01:14:37.562
Just do what you feel like.

274
01:14:41.562 --> 01:14:51.562
So you are saved, but you know, that is not the end of the story.

275
01:14:54.562 --> 01:14:58.562
Let me put it this way, it does not have to be the end of your story, in any case.

276
01:14:59.562 --> 01:15:02.562
But you know, you can make choices in that yourself.

277
01:15:03.562 --> 01:15:04.562
You may sit down.

278
01:15:05.562 --> 01:15:07.562
You can sit on the foundation.

279
01:15:08.562 --> 01:15:10.562
But I prefer to build.

280
01:15:13.562 --> 01:15:15.562
I want to be useful for the king.

281
01:15:18.562 --> 01:15:21.562
I want to honor the one who has saved me.

282
01:15:25.562 --> 01:15:28.562
I want to bring him glory on that day and no shame.

283
01:15:38.562 --> 01:15:50.562
He does not condemn me, but at that moment I will feel the shame of having made different choices.

284
01:15:51.562 --> 01:15:54.562
The choices I have made do not matter at all.

285
01:15:54.562 --> 01:15:56.562
And that is what causes me to feel that shame.

286
01:15:56.562 --> 01:16:01.562
Whether further building on that foundation is done with gold, silver, and precious stones.

287
01:16:12.562 --> 01:16:14.562
Or with wood, hay, and straw.

288
01:16:14.562 --> 01:16:17.562
I will not go into that today, but they are quite self-evident.

289
01:16:24.562 --> 01:16:28.562
Everyone's work will become clear what it is worth on that day.

290
01:16:35.562 --> 01:16:39.562
And on that day it will be fully revealed in the light.

291
01:16:39.562 --> 01:16:43.562
So it will become clear what you have built your life with.

292
01:16:45.562 --> 01:16:51.562
And it will be revealed by fire.

293
01:16:51.562 --> 01:16:55.562
And then we think back, his eyes are like fire.

294
01:17:00.562 --> 01:17:04.562
And the fire will show or test what each person's work is worth.

295
01:17:08.562 --> 01:17:11.562
If what someone has built stands firm.

296
01:17:14.562 --> 01:17:16.562
Then he will be rewarded.

297
01:17:20.562 --> 01:17:22.562
If the building burns down.

298
01:17:25.562 --> 01:17:28.562
Then the builder will pay the price for that.

299
01:17:30.562 --> 01:17:32.562
But he himself will be saved.

300
01:17:33.562 --> 01:17:34.562
Do you see that?

301
01:17:45.562 --> 01:17:47.562
So do you see that?

302
01:17:47.562 --> 01:17:51.562
The builder is saved, for the foundation stands firm.

303
01:17:51.562 --> 01:17:55.562
But then the materials you have used will be tested.

304
01:17:55.562 --> 01:17:56.562
And that is important.

305
01:18:00.562 --> 01:18:06.562
For the one who is saved, even though his work is burned up.

306
01:18:06.562 --> 01:18:09.562
He will be saved, but only as through fire.

307
01:18:09.562 --> 01:18:14.562
Let us go to Matthew 25 today.

308
01:18:18.562 --> 01:18:21.562
And this is a very well-known parable.

309
01:18:29.562 --> 01:18:32.562
The rewards are based on faithfulness.

310
01:18:33.562 --> 01:18:36.562
Faithfulness and availability for the Lord.

311
01:18:45.562 --> 01:18:53.562
That judgment for believers is about how you have lived.

312
01:18:56.562 --> 01:19:00.562
For something has been entrusted to you that is His.

313
01:19:03.562 --> 01:19:16.562
So on that day He will evaluate how you have used what you have received from Him to serve Him.

314
01:19:23.562 --> 01:19:30.562
And it will have a consequence regarding what is entrusted to you in the time of the kingdom.

315
01:19:33.562 --> 01:19:43.562
So the life you are living now is not without consequence; there is a direct connection to the time of the kingdom.

316
01:19:48.562 --> 01:19:52.562
How you build upon your salvation matters.

317
01:19:53.562 --> 01:19:55.562
And there will be a reward.

318
01:19:57.562 --> 01:20:00.562
And He does not reward you for the talents you have.

319
01:20:02.562 --> 01:20:17.562
I am not rewarded based on the talents I have; I am rewarded based on how I have used the talents I have received.

320
01:20:18.562 --> 01:20:19.562
What I have done with them.

321
01:20:19.562 --> 01:20:34.562
And we will see this very clearly in that story, but you all have a gift, there is something that the Lord has entrusted to you.

322
01:20:38.562 --> 01:20:40.562
And that gift is from Him.

323
01:20:50.562 --> 01:20:58.562
So it is not that gift, that talent itself, that determines what your reward is, that would make no sense.

324
01:20:59.562 --> 01:21:04.562
But what matters is how you have used that talent, that gift, and what you have done with it.

325
01:21:08.562 --> 01:21:09.562
Have I let it increase?

326
01:21:13.562 --> 01:21:15.562
Let's go to the story, for it explains itself.

327
01:21:20.562 --> 01:21:25.562
And you probably know this story, the story of the talents, the story of the bags of gold.

328
01:21:27.562 --> 01:21:28.562
And if you don't know it, that's okay.

329
01:21:33.562 --> 01:21:38.562
But what is important to know is that this is written in the context of His return.

330
01:21:50.562 --> 01:21:56.562
Jesus is here in a very extensive passage describing the kingdom and He describes the time when He will come back again.

331
01:21:59.562 --> 01:22:01.562
And as we begin at verse 14.

332
01:22:11.562 --> 01:22:14.562
If we start with that, it says again.

333
01:22:20.562 --> 01:22:24.562
And that means it links back to the story before and the story before that.

334
01:22:25.562 --> 01:22:29.562
The whole piece of teaching He is engaged in and the theme here is the kingdom will be like.

335
01:22:37.562 --> 01:22:39.562
It will be like a man who goes on a journey.

336
01:22:49.562 --> 01:22:53.562
He called his servants to him and gave them his money to manage.

337
01:23:06.562 --> 01:23:11.562
And you can underline that already and you can go on from there, for the man who is leaving is Jesus.

338
01:23:13.562 --> 01:23:14.562
He is going away.

339
01:23:20.562 --> 01:23:25.562
And He has called his servants to him and as He calls those servants, He entrusts them with something.

340
01:23:28.562 --> 01:23:30.562
Not only saved, but also entrusted.

341
01:23:37.562 --> 01:23:40.562
To one he gave five talents or five bags of gold.

342
01:23:42.562 --> 01:23:43.562
To another two.

343
01:23:45.562 --> 01:23:46.562
And to yet another one.

344
01:23:50.562 --> 01:23:52.562
Each according to his ability.

345
01:23:55.562 --> 01:23:56.562
How many times have you read this already?

346
01:24:01.562 --> 01:24:05.562
Very often we read this and simply start comparing the numbers.

347
01:24:05.562 --> 01:24:13.562
Jesus, why do they get five and he gets two? You are so harmless, why does he get more than I do?

348
01:24:14.562 --> 01:24:15.562
Comparing.

349
01:24:21.562 --> 01:24:28.562
But God in His wisdom and in His grace tells why He does this. He says, I give according to my ability.

350
01:24:36.562 --> 01:24:40.562
Did you know that it is not all equal in the kingdom?

351
01:24:43.562 --> 01:24:44.562
That is already true.

352
01:24:47.562 --> 01:24:50.562
And what was true in the time of the kingdom is also true now.

353
01:24:56.562 --> 01:25:01.562
And what you have is not exactly the same as everyone around you.

354
01:25:03.562 --> 01:25:04.562
That is a distraction.

355
01:25:06.562 --> 01:25:11.562
To get caught up in competition and comparison, that is a distraction.

356
01:25:16.562 --> 01:25:20.562
And in His grace, He will not give you things that you cannot bear.

357
01:25:20.562 --> 01:25:37.562
So here too, do not look around and think, I would like to have what he or she has. You are wasting your time with that.

358
01:25:43.562 --> 01:25:46.562
Just do what He has given you to do.

359
01:25:51.562 --> 01:25:56.562
For if you get caught up in that comparison and competition, then you will not be on the right path.

360
01:26:01.562 --> 01:26:04.562
And then you lose your own reward, for you have wasted time.

361
01:26:06.562 --> 01:26:08.562
He is full of grace for you.

362
01:26:09.562 --> 01:26:11.562
He is so gracious towards you.

363
01:26:13.562 --> 01:26:15.562
He is loving towards you.

364
01:26:21.562 --> 01:26:26.562
He has entrusted you with nothing that you cannot increase in His grace.

365
01:26:28.562 --> 01:26:29.562
So get to work.

366
01:26:34.562 --> 01:26:38.562
Whatever He has given you, it is time to start running with it.

367
01:26:42.562 --> 01:26:45.562
For He has given you all the possibilities to bear fruit.

368
01:26:46.562 --> 01:26:48.562
And He longs to give you a reward.

369
01:26:56.562 --> 01:26:57.562
And then He left.

370
01:27:02.562 --> 01:27:06.562
I have saved you, I have entrusted things to you, I am off for a while.

371
01:27:15.562 --> 01:27:20.562
This is the time we are living in. We are between the first and the second coming.

372
01:27:24.562 --> 01:27:27.562
So He is going away for a very long time.

373
01:27:34.562 --> 01:27:38.562
And the man who received five bags of gold went straight to work.

374
01:27:38.562 --> 01:27:43.562
And he put his money to work and earned five more bags of gold.

375
01:27:50.562 --> 01:27:51.562
Verse 17

376
01:27:59.562 --> 01:28:05.562
And in the same way, the man who received two bags of gold earned two more.

377
01:28:09.562 --> 01:28:19.562
So whether you look at the man with five or with two bags, it is a hundredfold return.

378
01:28:23.562 --> 01:28:26.562
Did they not both double?

379
01:28:26.562 --> 01:28:27.562
Doubled?

380
01:28:35.562 --> 01:28:38.562
Essentially, they both did the same thing.

381
01:28:45.562 --> 01:28:48.562
One started with five and went to work.

382
01:28:48.562 --> 01:28:53.562
And the one who started with two did not worry about the other.

383
01:28:53.562 --> 01:28:56.562
He simply went to work with his two bags of gold.

384
01:28:58.562 --> 01:29:00.562
And then in verse 18, but.

385
01:29:07.562 --> 01:29:13.562
You just heard two nice stories and then the word but appears, then it is time to pay attention to that.

386
01:29:14.562 --> 01:29:15.562
Pay attention.

387
01:29:17.562 --> 01:29:19.562
Because now something different is happening.

388
01:29:24.562 --> 01:29:33.562
But the one who had received one talent, one bag of gold, went away.

389
01:29:39.562 --> 01:29:48.562
In English it says that the first two went straight to work and here it says this one walked aside or something.

390
01:29:54.562 --> 01:30:01.562
And that already paints a picture and that is sad.

391
01:30:04.562 --> 01:30:07.562
He went on his way.

392
01:30:11.562 --> 01:30:14.562
He dug a hole in the ground.

393
01:30:14.562 --> 01:30:24.562
He dug a hole in the ground and hid his master's money.

394
01:30:26.562 --> 01:30:28.562
And this is a very depressing picture.

395
01:30:31.562 --> 01:30:33.562
But he went away.

396
01:30:35.562 --> 01:30:37.562
And you feel that it is already different.

397
01:30:39.562 --> 01:30:41.562
There is something not right with this servant.

398
01:30:42.562 --> 01:30:43.562
He has been saved.

399
01:30:44.562 --> 01:30:45.562
He has been set free.

400
01:30:47.562 --> 01:30:49.562
And something has been entrusted to him.

401
01:30:50.562 --> 01:30:51.562
And yet he went away.

402
01:30:52.562 --> 01:30:53.562
And he dug a hole.

403
01:30:54.562 --> 01:30:55.562
And he hid it.

404
01:31:02.562 --> 01:31:12.562
And after a long time, after a long time, the master or the lord of those servants returned.

405
01:31:12.562 --> 01:31:13.562
He came.

406
01:31:14.562 --> 01:31:15.562
He came back.

407
01:31:18.562 --> 01:31:20.562
And he asked them for an account.

408
01:31:20.562 --> 01:31:22.562
They went to settle the accounts.

409
01:31:26.562 --> 01:31:28.562
And the man who went on a journey, that is Jesus.

410
01:31:32.562 --> 01:31:37.562
And he calls his servants to him and entrusts them with something.

411
01:31:37.562 --> 01:31:44.562
And the meantime is the time in which you are tested.

412
01:31:56.562 --> 01:32:05.562
And you could say that your life now, that this time we are living here, is one big test of what the lord can entrust to you in the time to come.

413
01:32:07.562 --> 01:32:21.562
Knowing that he has gone, but also knowing that he would come back, what can I do with what he has entrusted to me?

414
01:32:27.562 --> 01:32:31.562
The one who had received five bags of gold took the other five with him.

415
01:32:32.562 --> 01:32:39.562
And he says, lord, you have entrusted me with five talents.

416
01:32:42.562 --> 01:32:44.562
Here you go, I have earned five more.

417
01:32:48.562 --> 01:32:52.562
And the lord said to him, excellent, you are a good and faithful servant.

418
01:32:56.562 --> 01:33:00.562
And what you can highlight here is faithfulness.

419
01:33:01.562 --> 01:33:24.562
And that faithfulness does not lie in how many talents someone has been entrusted with, but in how those talents have been used and whether they are available.

420
01:33:32.562 --> 01:33:42.562
Because you have proven to be faithful with a few things, in the management of a small amount.

421
01:33:49.562 --> 01:33:59.562
Those who have received the most have still only been entrusted with a few small things in the eyes of Jesus.

422
01:34:00.562 --> 01:34:01.562
Do you see that?

423
01:34:02.562 --> 01:34:03.562
It's not about big things.

424
01:34:05.562 --> 01:34:06.562
Your words.

425
01:34:10.562 --> 01:34:15.562
The influence you have within your family, among your friends, it's about those small things.

426
01:34:17.562 --> 01:34:20.562
It often doesn't concern the big things.

427
01:34:21.562 --> 01:34:25.562
It's your money, it's your time, it's your energy, it's the gift, both natural and spiritual.

428
01:34:28.562 --> 01:34:34.562
It's your money, it's your time, it's your energy, it's the things you have in the spiritual and in the material.

429
01:34:35.562 --> 01:34:38.562
It's all about that, but it often lies in the small things.

430
01:34:50.562 --> 01:35:03.562
And you often see that reflected, the Spirit gives you things and He looks at how you handle them and whether He can trust you with them.

431
01:35:07.562 --> 01:35:09.562
But it's your faith to get started with that.

432
01:35:11.562 --> 01:35:12.562
It's not about big things.

433
01:35:20.562 --> 01:35:27.562
It's that you feel like praying for someone and you go to that person and you say be blessed.

434
01:35:28.562 --> 01:35:30.562
And that is faith in action.

435
01:35:30.562 --> 01:35:56.562
And today I want to remove the idea that it’s about very big and powerful things, because for many of us it’s precisely about those very small everyday things.

436
01:36:00.562 --> 01:36:04.562
And all we need to do is look at them in the right way.

437
01:36:09.562 --> 01:36:12.562
For He says it's just a few small things, it was just a small amount.

438
01:36:15.562 --> 01:36:16.562
And then Jesus says this.

439
01:36:22.562 --> 01:36:26.562
Because you have proven to be trustworthy, I will appoint you over much.

440
01:36:28.562 --> 01:36:29.562
Many things.

441
01:36:31.562 --> 01:36:34.562
So the exchange rate is really high.

442
01:36:37.562 --> 01:36:39.562
In this life, you have a few things.

443
01:36:42.562 --> 01:36:44.562
And how you use them for the King.

444
01:36:48.562 --> 01:36:51.562
That will mean that when you stand before the throne of judgment.

445
01:37:01.562 --> 01:37:03.562
But he says, no idea.

446
01:37:10.562 --> 01:37:15.562
Then you will see that he says my son or my daughter, I have seen how you have gotten to work.

447
01:37:16.562 --> 01:37:22.562
Not always, there are moments, but I have seen how you have been busy in faith.

448
01:37:23.562 --> 01:37:24.562
And I will give you many things.

449
01:37:27.562 --> 01:37:28.562
Good exchange rate.

450
01:37:30.562 --> 01:37:32.562
Jesus is exuberant.

451
01:37:36.562 --> 01:37:40.562
And Jesus is really interested in giving you that reward.

452
01:37:44.562 --> 01:37:48.562
And in the time to come, you will be grateful that you have been faithful.

453
01:37:53.562 --> 01:37:57.562
For then he says come and share in the joy of your master.

454
01:38:01.562 --> 01:38:03.562
You didn't really have to give a reward, Jesus.

455
01:38:03.562 --> 01:38:05.562
Just cool to be there. You will not be like that, believe me.

456
01:38:05.562 --> 01:38:08.562
For those who think, this is not for me, I don't like rewards.

457
01:38:08.562 --> 01:38:09.562
You love rewards.

458
01:38:09.562 --> 01:38:11.562
He is the one who wants to give it.

459
01:38:11.562 --> 01:38:12.562
You love rewards.

460
01:38:12.562 --> 01:38:13.562
Because he gives it.

461
01:38:22.562 --> 01:38:23.562
It is not even true.

462
01:38:23.562 --> 01:38:25.562
We are so complicated.

463
01:38:25.562 --> 01:38:27.562
This is how we are made.

464
01:38:33.562 --> 01:38:40.562
He rewards faithfulness and you will enter into a joy, a delight with Him like you have never experienced before.

465
01:38:45.562 --> 01:38:50.562
If Jesus Himself has taught about this, then I want to be there.

466
01:38:51.562 --> 01:38:55.562
And I do not want to cast it aside as if it is not important.

467
01:38:58.562 --> 01:39:01.562
Or pretend that it does not really matter to me.

468
01:39:02.562 --> 01:39:04.562
That is not the right attitude.

469
01:39:06.562 --> 01:39:08.562
That is more the attitude of another servant.

470
01:39:12.562 --> 01:39:16.562
